Reproduction patch for arc-swap Family-5 generation-wrap panic.

This patch is applied on top of the round-4 working tree (which already
contains the tla_trace harness emit calls).  It adds:

  1. src/debt/helping.rs : two #[cfg(test)] hooks on `Local` and `Slots`:
       - Local::seed_generation_for_test  — pre-load the per-thread
         generation counter to a chosen value
       - Slots::reset_for_test            — reset the helping slot's
         control word back to IDLE (used by the test for cleanup so the
         dirty slot left by the panic doesn't cascade-fail subsequent
         tests claiming the same node).
     Production builds are unaffected because both impls are gated by
     `#[cfg(test)]`.

  2. src/debt/list.rs    : a unit test
     `confirm_helping_panic_after_generation_wrap` in the existing
     `mod tests` block.  The test:
       a) Seeds the generation to `usize::MAX & !3` so the next
          `wrapping_add(4)` overflows to 0.
       b) Calls `LocalNode::new_helping`, which fires `discard = true`,
          runs `start_cooldown` + `self.node.take()`.
       c) Calls `LocalNode::confirm_helping`, which panics on the literal
          `expect("LocalNode::with ensures it is set")` at
          `src/debt/list.rs:313`.
     `catch_unwind` captures the panic, then `Node::traverse` resets
     every helping slot's control via `reset_for_test`.

The seeding is Level-2 state injection per the bug-confirmation skill:
the per-thread generation counter is private and the natural path to
wrap (2^62 calls per thread on 64-bit, 2^30 on 32-bit) is impractical
in a test.  All other state — node allocation, cooldown lifecycle,
helping-slot control swap — runs unmodified through the public
LocalNode interface.

To reproduce, run from the repro/ dir:
  ./test_bug1_run.sh

Or directly:
  cd /home/ubuntu/Specula/case-studies/arc-swap_4/artifact/arc-swap
  cargo test --lib confirm_helping_panic_after_generation_wrap -- \
    --nocapture --test-threads=1

Expected output: "thread '...' panicked at src/debt/list.rs:313:37:
                  LocalNode::with ensures it is set"

